OpenMesh firmware — third-party notices
========================================

This firmware is AGPL-3.0-or-later. It builds with PlatformIO and includes or links the
following components. Pin maps are our own files derived from publicly documented hardware; the
sources we cross-checked are cited per board and do not transfer Meshtastic application code.

Vendored source (in firmware/lib/openmesh/third_party/)
-------------------------------------------------------
* Monocypher 4.0.2 — Loup Vaillant, Michael Savage, Fabio Scotoni.
  Files: monocypher.c, monocypher.h, monocypher-ed25519.c, monocypher-ed25519.h, LICENCE.md.
  Dual-licensed BSD-2-Clause OR CC0-1.0. Provides X25519 and XChaCha20-Poly1305. The optional
  monocypher-ed25519 module (RFC 8032 SHA-512 Ed25519) is used because Monocypher's default
  EdDSA uses BLAKE2b and is NOT wire-compatible with ed25519-dalek on the Rust side.
  https://github.com/LoupVaillant/Monocypher (tag 4.0.2)
* SHA-256 / HMAC-SHA256 / HKDF-SHA256 — OpenMesh contributors (firmware/lib/openmesh/src/om_sha256.c),
  AGPL-3.0-or-later, validated against FIPS 180-4, RFC 4231 and RFC 5869 vectors.

PlatformIO libraries (resolved from lib_deps, not vendored)
------------------------------------------------------------
* RadioLib (jgromes/RadioLib) — MIT — SX126x/LR11x0 radio drivers.
* NimBLE-Arduino (h2zero) — Apache-2.0 — BLE stack for ESP32-S3. The ESP32-S3 BLE stack
  (Apache NimBLE) is Apache-2.0.
* Adafruit nRF52 Arduino core (via the Meshtastic platform fork) — LGPL-2.1 — nRF52 core,
  TinyUSB CDC, Bluefruit BLE, InternalFileSystem.
* Arduino-ESP32 core (espressif32 platform) — LGPL-2.1 — ESP32-S3 core, LittleFS.
* Adafruit TinyUSB / TinyUSB — MIT — USB CDC.

Hardware references (facts and pin values re-expressed in our own headers)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Seeed SenseCAP T1000-E — vendor Arduino variant and Seeed open-source hardware documentation.
* RAK WisBlock RAK4631 / RAK4630 — RAKwireless datasheet and variant pin definitions.
* Seeed SenseCAP Solar Node P1 — vendor variant definitions and Seeed documentation.
* Heltec Wireless Tracker V1.1 — Heltec schematic and vendor variant definitions.
